items.fromString:
The Streams for Apache Kafka cluster operator pod is intermittently crashing, which is blocking the reconciliation of our Kafka cluster instances. The crash is a fatal native JVM segmentation fault ({{SIGSEGV}}) occurring inside the bundled OpenJDK 21 runtime, specifically in the {{libjvm.so}} library.

The crash happens at the native frame {{markWord::displaced_mark_helper() const+0x1a}}. This points to a known HotSpot concurrency/locking bug, where the JVM misreads memory during lightweight lock inflation/deflation (closely matching upstream behavior reported for ARM in JDK-8327647).

{{# A fatal error has been detected by the Java Runtime Environment: # #  SIGSEGV (0xb) at pc=0x000003ffa2fc072a, pid=16, tid=4079 # # JRE version: OpenJDK Runtime Environment (Red_Hat-21.0.11.0.10-1) (21.0.11+10) (build 21.0.11+10-LTS) # Java VM: OpenJDK 64-Bit Server VM (Red_Hat-21.0.11.0.10-1) (21.0.11+10-LTS, mixed mode, sharing, tiered, compressed oops, compressed class ptrs, serial gc, linux-s390x) # Problematic frame: # V  [libjvm.so+0x94072a]  markWord::displaced_mark_helper() const+0x1a # # Core dump will be written. Default location: Core dumps may be processed with "/usr/lib/systemd/systemd-coredump %P %u %g %s %t %c %h" (or dumping to /opt/strimzi/core.16) # # An error report file with more information is saved as: # /tmp/hs_err_pid16.log [204.431s][warning][os] Loading hsdis library failed}}

